To handle 20-digit numbers with 4 decimal places without falling into scientific notation () or losing precision, you must avoid using `Double` or `Float`. In Java, the senior-standard for financial precision is **`BigDecimal`**.

When Jackson serializes `BigDecimal`, it can still sometimes trigger scientific notation depending on the configuration. We will fix this in the **Model**, the **Query**, and the **Service**.

### 1. Update the Model

Ensure the `profitLoss` field in your `PLTransfer` entity uses `BigDecimal`.

**File:** `com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.model.PLTransfer.java`

```java
@Column(name = "PROFIT_LOSS", precision = 25, scale = 4)
private BigDecimal profitLoss; 

```

