### 2. Update the Repository (Native Query)

The native query needs to return `BigDecimal` from the `SUM` function. Most modern DB drivers (Oracle/PostgreSQL) do this automatically for `SUM`.

**File:** `com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.repository.PLTransferRepository.java`

```java
@Query(value = "SELECT CIRCLE_BRANCH_CODE, SUM(PROFIT_LOSS) " +
               "FROM P_L_TRANSFER " +
               "GROUP BY CIRCLE_BRANCH_CODE", nativeQuery = true)
List<Object[]> getAggregatedSummary();

```

---

### 3. Updated Service Implementation (Optimized for Precision)

We will change the `Map` to use `String` keys and **`BigDecimal`** values. To force Jackson to avoid scientific notation in the final JSON, we can configure the `ObjectMapper` or use `toPlainString()`.

**File:** `com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.service.CommonMasterServiceImpl.java`

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public Object getOrGenerateLhoSummary(Long id) {
    // 1. Check Cache... (Existing logic)

    // 2. Fetch Aggregation
    List<Object[]> results = plTransferRepository.getAggregatedSummary();
    
    // 3. Use Map<String, BigDecimal> to maintain 20-digit precision
    Map<String, BigDecimal> summaryMap = new HashMap<>();
    
    for (Object[] row : results) {
        String code = String.valueOf(row[0]);
        // Cast directly to BigDecimal to preserve precision from DB
        BigDecimal sum = (row[1] != null) ? new BigDecimal(row[1].toString()) : BigDecimal.ZERO;
        
        // Force 4 decimal places
        summaryMap.put(code, sum.setScale(4, RoundingMode.HALF_UP));
    }

    try {
        // 4. Save to CLOB as a plain string (no scientific notation)
        String jsonPayload = objectMapper.writeValueAsString(summaryMap);
        lhoSummaryRepository.save(new LhoTransferSummary(id, jsonPayload));
        
        return summaryMap;
    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error("Precision error", e);
        throw new RuntimeException("Summary generation failed");
    }
}

```

